// Worked example: fillet only top-face edges via topology-relational selectors
// PRD: docs/prds/topology-selectors.md task 7
//
// Demonstrates the topology-relational selectors from §3.9: pick the single
// upward-facing face of a box, walk its adjacent faces, collect the edges shared
// with each adjacent face, and fillet only those (the four top-perimeter edges).
//
// Coverage:
//   1. faces_by_normal(solid, direction, tol) + single() → top-face selection
//   2. flat_map(adjacent_faces(solid, face), |f| shared_edges(face, f)) →
//      walk topology to collect the perimeter edges of the chosen face
//   3. fillet(solid, edges, radius) → apply the fillet to the curated edge set
//
// Capability status: LIVE and designer-reachable end-to-end. 3-arg
// `fillet(solid, edges, radius)` — the compiler stdlib binding
// (`crates/reify-compiler/src/geometry_modify.rs`,
// `"fillet" => match compiled_args.len() { 2 | 3 => ... }`), the
// `GeometryOp::Fillet` `edges` field, and in-loop curated-fillet dispatch
// (selector→op build) — landed via #3205 and #4360; the UnifiedDag default
// flip landed via #4362. #5208 closed the last reachability gap: curated
// 3-arg fillet now builds through the PRODUCTION .ri pipeline (`reify eval`
// and the GUI) — not only through hand-driven `engine.build(UnifiedDag)`
// harnesses — and a genuinely unresolvable selector now surfaces as an
// actionable designer diagnostic instead of a stale "not yet available"
// message. `single`, `flat_map`, `faces_by_normal`, `adjacent_faces`, and
// `shared_edges` were already landed before that (task 2698/2699). This
// example is NOT a phantom capability gap — it demonstrates the v0.1 design
// vision end-to-end: fillet only the four top-perimeter edges via
// topology-relational selection, rather than filleting all edges of the box
// (which the 2-arg form would do, defeating the example's pedagogic purpose).
//
// Real-kernel end-to-end coverage (real OCCT kernel + UnifiedDag scheduler)
// lives in crates/reify-eval/tests/fillet_curated_edges_e2e.rs:
//
//   * fillet_curated_edges_3205_e2e — curated-vs-fillet-all volume contrast.
//     It selects edges with `edges_at_height`; it does NOT drive this file's
//     faces_by_normal → single → adjacent_faces → shared_edges → flat_map
//     chain (an earlier revision of this header claimed it did — it never
//     has; corrected by #5208).
//   * bottom_deck_selectors_example_builds_clean_e2e — production-build e2e
//     over examples/topology_selectors/bottom_deck_selectors.ri (7 curated
//     fillets: edges_parallel_to on blank lets, a boolean-result parent, and
//     chained named-let stages). The same example is driven through the CLI
//     entry point by crates/reify-cli/tests/harness_cli/cli_eval_geometry.rs.
//
// The topology-walk chain used by THIS file is covered at the parse and
// compile tiers (below); its real-kernel eval coverage is still open (#4727).
//
// Smoke-test coverage tiers in
//   crates/reify-eval/tests/harness_topology_selector/topology_selector_smoke_tests.rs:
//
//   parse               → active (fillet_top_edges_ri_parses_cleanly)
//   compile-with-stdlib → active (fillet_top_edges_compiles_with_stdlib_no_errors)
//                         — un-ignored by #5208. This file is also no longer
//                         in the SKIP_SET of
//                         crates/reify-compiler/tests/harness_compilation_surface/examples_smoke.rs,
//                         so the bulk walker compiles it too.
//   eval (bare MockGeometryKernel) → #[ignore] (fillet_top_edges_evals_to_solid_via_topology_walk)
//                         — still blocked on #4727 (pending): the bare mock
//                         kernel records only the Box op and never reaches
//                         Fillet, so the topology walk needs a real-OCCT +
//                         set_build_scheduler(UnifiedDag) rewrite (re-verified
//                         2026-07-26 with `--ignored`). That capability is
//                         covered by the two e2e tests above.

structure def FilletTopEdges {
    let b = box(50mm, 30mm, 10mm)
    let top = single(faces_by_normal(b, vec3(0.0, 0.0, 1.0), 1deg))
    let top_edges = flat_map(adjacent_faces(b, top), |f| shared_edges(top, f))
    let result = fillet(b, top_edges, 1mm)
}
